Explanation:
• Field_4 currently has the highest bird‐threat (0.21) and needs 3 drones for full protection. We assign the three drones already en‐route (Drone_2, Drone_3, Drone_6) to Field_4.
• Field_2 is next in priority (threat 0.10) and requires 4 drones; with Drone_4 already protecting it we reassign three drones from the surplus on Field_1 (Drone_1, Drone_5, Drone_7) so that Field_2 becomes fully protected.
• This leaves Drone_8 from Field_1’s original crew unassigned. Given that Field_1 has the lowest threat (0.05) and Field_3 (threat 0.09) is completely unprotected, we put the spare drone on Field_3 where one drone will at least partially mitigate the damage, while leaving Field_1 unprotected.
In this way the fields with the highest bird‐threat get full protection while the less critical ones get, if possible, some measure of cover.
